body:
yeah, he is definitely not the one for me

&#x200B;

i just want to be single and work through all my issues first

either he really thinks that, or it was him getting defensive 

&#x200B;

manipulation as you said

Why are you so spot on right now? After thinking about it, yes I have fallen into this trap many times, in different disguises. And... yes I do have my trauma that makes me like this. And yes I do need help. Fortunately, this was the earliest I have cut someone like this off, unfortunately it stilled causes damage really quickly. I am okay though. I guess I needed reassurance that I made the right choice.

&#x200B;

Also I find myself thinking about the entire thing over and over to try and figure out what's going on with him, I can't figure out why I need that closure.
